#lang rmn/v2
(map
  ("type" "FiniteInfomaterialPatchObservationLaw")
  ("version" 7)
  ("precondition" "A customer supplies one absolute regular-file, symbolic-link, or directory patch, finite entry and byte ceilings, and an exact unexpired single-use capability bound to the provider-authored offer; the provider establishes its own smart-account binding and contracted witness-journal RDF seam before reading the patch. No exclusion or traversal policy is caller selectable, and no request may claim the patch is the whole territory.")
  ("operation" "Read every entry in that one patch without following symbolic links; hash every regular-file byte stream; construct placement-neutral typed RMN material identities bottom-up, binding names only at containing-directory and occurrence faces; detect concurrent mutation within the patch; and prepare a sorted blank-node-free RDF topology before placing it.")
  ("postcondition" "Return one canonical RMN-identified patch observation containing the exact placement-neutral patch material identity, root kind, complete patch-local counts and byte measures, and a SHA-256 identified canonical N-Quads patch topology; append the provider receipt through witness-journal RDF, or roll back the newly placed artifact if preparation, placement, or receipt fails. The result makes no conductor, global-instant, territorial-cover, or descent claim.")
  ("refusal" "Refuse before observation when the canonical smart-account binding or contracted witness-journal RDF seam is absent; otherwise refuse a relative patch, a root other than a regular file, symbolic link, or directory, caller-selected exclusion or traversal semantics, a whole-territory atomicity claim, scratch storage inside the observed patch, missing or mismatched capability, resource-ceiling breach, unsupported filesystem material, unreadable entry, concurrent mutation, foreign mutation authority, incomplete topology projection, or partial success presented as a complete patch observation."))
